tps://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b59acd73249e0b9e1cc3b64c79748f37?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-1.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b59acd73249e0b9e1cc3b64c79748f37?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-1.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b59acd73249e0b9e1cc3b64c79748f37?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-1.png"},"displayName":"Chris Ward","active":true,"timeZone":"America/Bogota","accountType":"atlassian"},"created":"2026-10-14T14:13:39.595-0500","size":213019,"mimeType":"image/png","content":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/attachment/content/62329","thumbnail":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/attachment/thumbnail/62329"},{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/attachment/62330","id":"62330","filename":"D1-design-tech_view-1440.png","author":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/user?accountId=712020%3Aaa00b8d6-a71f-4259-8919-82a304227c20","accountId":"712020:aa00b8d6-a71f-4259-8919-82a304227c20","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b59acd73249e0b9e1cc3b64c79748f37?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-1.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b59acd73249e0b9e1cc3b64c79748f37?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-1.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b59acd73249e0b9e1cc3b64c79748f37?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-1.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b59acd73249e0b9e1cc3b64c79748f37?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-1.png"},"displayName":"Chris Ward","active":true,"timeZone":"America/Bogota","accountType":"atlassian"},"created":"2026-10-14T14:13:40.825-0500","size":176983,"mimeType":"image/png","content":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/attachment/content/62330","thumbnail":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/attachment/thumbnail/62330"}],"description":"h3. What\n\nTech View opens on the design's default columns instead of the List's production defaults.\n\nh3. Expected\n\nS5-R4: \"Until the user changes Tech View's columns, Tech View shows these columns, in this order, as in the design: Status, Waiting On Parts, Number, Customer, Unit, Asset, Progress, Service Advisor, Clocked In, Lines, Assigned Techs, Created on, Total price (Total price subject to financial permission). On Site, VIN/Serial # and Lead Technician are off by default; each can be added with the column chooser (S2-R4). List's columns are unchanged.\" S7-R7: Assigned Techs is on by default and can be removed.\n\nPRD: [Board View & Tech View PRD v51|https://shopview.atlassian.net/wiki/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=845185030] (S5-R4, S7-R7).\n\nh3. Actual (staging build, develop b19269d4487, clicked through locally)\n\nTech View shows the List's 14 columns (On Site, Status, Number, Customer, Asset, Unit, VIN/Serial #, Progress, Service Advisor, Lead Technician, Clocked In, Lines, Total Price, Created On). Lead Technician repeats the group's technician on every row.\n\nh3. How to check\n\n* A user who has never changed Tech View's columns sees exactly the 13 columns above, in that order.\n* On Site, VIN/Serial # and Lead Technician can still be added from the column chooser.\n* Total price is hidden for users without financial permission.\n* List's columns are unchanged.\n\nh3. Screenshots\n\nAttached: staging build first, Branko's design (files starting D) after.\n\nRaised from Sasha's staging review, 2026-10-14.\n\n----\n\n*Test cases for this design issue:*\n\n* [C590113|https://shopview.testrail.io/index.php?/cases/view/590113] Tech View opens on 13 default columns with small grey header labels\n* [C590112|https://shopview.testrail.io/index.php?/cases/view/590112] Tech View table runs edge to edge on white with no side gutter\n* [C590126|https://shopview.testrail.io/index.php?/cases/view/590126] No labels overlap in the toolbar and headers from 1024 to 1920 px wide\n* [C96979|https://shopview.testrail.io/index.php?/cases/view/96979] A new user's Tech View opens on the design's 13 columns\n* [C96927|https://shopview.testrail.io/index.php?/cases/view/96927] Tech View offers List's columns plus Assigned Techs in its own Columns menu\n\nh3. PRD v54 update (2026-10-15)\n\n* S2-R22: when the columns are wider than the screen, Tech View scrolls sideways, as in the design; columns keep the design's minimum widths and are never squeezed or clipped. Sideways scrolling at 1440px is not a defect.\n* S5-R4: headings use the List's labels for List columns (Unit, not Unit #) and Assigned Techs for the new column.\n* S5-R4a: Status, Number and Customer are always shown in Tech View and cannot be turned off; every other column, Unit included, can be.\n\nAlso check:\n\n* At 1440px the table scrolls sideways with no column squeezed or clipped.\n* Headings read Unit and Assigned Techs.\n* Status, Number and Customer cannot be turned off in the column chooser; Unit can.","reporter":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/user?accountId=712020%3Aaa00b8d6-a71f-4259-8919-82a304227c20","accountId":"712020:aa00b8d6-a71f-4259-8919-82a304227c20","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b59acd73249e0b9e1cc3b64c79748f37?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-1.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b59acd73249e0b9e1cc3b64c79748f37?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-1.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b59acd73249e0b9e1cc3b64c79748f37?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-1.png","32x